+# Working in this repo with Rojo
+
+Git is the source of truth. The place is built from the files in this repo, and `rojo serve`
+pushes them into your own dev place in Studio. The Layout table in [README.md](../README.md)
+shows which folder becomes which instance.
+
+## First-time setup
+
+1. Install the tools with `rokit install`, then install the packages with `pesde install` (and
+   again in `test_packages/`). `roblox_packages/` and `sourcemap.json` are generated and
+   git-ignored, so a fresh clone doesn't have them.
+2. Make your own dev place in Studio (a copy of the Baseplate is fine). Don't serve into a shared
+   or published place.
+3. Install the Rojo plugin that matches the CLI: `rojo plugin install`. The plugin and the CLI
+   (7.7.1, pinned in `rokit.toml`) have to speak the same protocol version.
+
+## Day to day
+
+1. Pull, then run `pesde install` if `pesde.toml` or `pesde.lock` changed.
+2. Start `rojo serve` from the repo root. It listens on port 34872 (`servePort` in
+   `default.project.json`). In your dev place, click **Connect** in the Rojo plugin.
+3. Edit files in your editor. Each save syncs into Studio.
+4. Commit on your own branch, and open a pull request.
+
+## Make every change in files
+
+- Edit scripts as `.luau` files under `src/`, never in Studio's script editor. The next sync
+  overwrites a Studio edit, and Git never sees it.
+- The same goes for attributes, tags, and properties on synced instances: put them in a
+  `.meta.json` beside the file (or `init.meta.json` in a folder). Service settings and the
+  Baseplate live in `default.project.json`.
+- Use Studio to read, run specs, and playtest. Treat anything you change there as throwaway.
+- Never edit files under `roblox_packages/` or `test_packages/roblox_packages/`: pesde replaces
+  them on every install, and they're hardlinked to a store other projects share. Require packages
+  through their links (`ReplicatedStorage.Packages.Vide`), never through a `.pesde/...` path.
+- Jest specs go in `src/ServerScriptService/Tests/Specs` as `Name.spec.luau`.
+
+## What to check while serving
+
+- **Rojo is still running.** Rojo 7.7.x crashes when a file or folder is deleted, moved, or
+  renamed (`Rojo crashed!` in its terminal), and Studio then silently stops getting changes. After
+  any delete or rename, glance at the terminal. If it crashed, restart `rojo serve` and click
+  Connect again.
+- **Your change actually arrived.** Open the script in Studio and confirm it has the new text
+  before you trust a playtest or a spec run. If an error's line number didn't move with your
+  edit, you're running old code.
+- **You're serving the right checkout.** Studio runs whatever the connected server serves: the
+  folder it started in, on the branch checked out there.
+- **Stop `rojo serve` first** before a `git checkout`/`switch`/`pull`/`rebase`/`stash`,
+  `pesde install`, or a bulk delete, and restart it afterward.
+- Before pushing, run the checks in the README (sourcemap, `luau-lsp analyze`, `selene`,
+  `stylua --check`).
+
+## Don't break the project file again
+
+`default.project.json` decides where everything lands. A bad merge there can break sourcemaps,
+types, and Jest for everyone.
+
+- **Resolving a conflict in it:** don't just keep both sides. Compare the result against the
+  Layout table in the README, row by row. Every row needs exactly one mount at exactly that path.
+- **Pay attention to these mounts, which are easy to break:**
+  - `test_packages/roblox_packages` mounts at `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages`, not under
+    `ReplicatedStorage`. The specs require Jest from there.
+  - `Tests` mounts `src/ServerScriptService/Tests` with `Packages` as a child, and
+    `globIgnorePaths` keeps that folder out of the `ServerScriptService` mount. Remove either one
+    and you get a duplicate or a missing `Tests` folder.
+  - Folder names have to match the disk exactly (`StarterPlayerScripts`, with the `s`). A `$path`
+    to a folder that doesn't exist fails the sourcemap.
+- **Save it as UTF-8 without a BOM.** Rojo rejects a project file that starts with a byte order
+  mark ("Failed to parse JSONC"). Windows PowerShell 5.1's `Set-Content` and `Out-File`, and some
+  merge tools, add one. In VS Code, use **Save with Encoding → UTF-8**.
+- **Verify before you commit:** run
+  `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`. It has to
+  succeed, and `sourcemap.json` should show `ServerScriptService.Tests.Specs`,
+  `ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest`, and `ReplicatedStorage.Packages` where the README
+  says. Then run `luau-lsp analyze`.
+- To lock serving to your own dev place, you can add its id to `servePlaceIds` in the project
+  file. Rojo then refuses to sync into any other place.
